Subject: =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=96=90=EF=B8=8F=20Turn=20off=20two-finger=20swipe?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20navigation=20in=20Settings?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
Add the client-only historySwipeNavigation boolean, defaulting to true so
existing swipe navigation stays enabled until the user turns it off.
Expose Swipe to go back and forward in General > Navigation on desktop,
with explanatory mouse-wheel copy, a reset action, restore-defaults support,
and desktop-only Settings search terms.

Only mount HistorySwipeNavigation when Electron and the preference are both
enabled. Turning it off removes the indicator and wheel/gesture listeners,
including during an active swipe. Turning it back on takes effect immediately.
Keep mouse back/forward buttons and keyboard history commands unchanged.

Integration details:
- Also gate upstream native macOS swipe events using the current persisted client preference; ignore vertical gestures, preserve available-history checks, and avoid navigation after the window closes during the asynchronous settings read. Settings read failures are logged without navigation. The shared contracts schema preserves the key through desktop IPC and disk persistence.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. 965ddc1d6c has no swipe preference: DesktopWindow.ts and AppSidebarLayout.tsx did not change upstream and still navigate unconditionally. Upstream #33131 and #33147 reshaped SettingsPanels.tsx, settingsSearch.ts and settings.ts; the Navigation section, restore entry, search item and schema field merged beside them.

Port to 691b9709b0:
- Upstream 4363d0bf65 (#32963) makes HistorySwipeNavigation listen on macOS only; the layout test reports a macOS platform so it runs on any host, as upstream 42185a6206 did for its own swipe test

